How to start Docker
bash
docker-compose up
No --build needed unless you changed code. Just up.


To stop Docker:
bash# Ctrl+C  — if running in foreground
# Or if running in background
docker-compose down


Never run docker-compose down -v 
unless you want to completely reset the database. 
Just docker-compose down is always safe.


Quick rule:
Changed code → docker-compose up --build
No changes → docker-compose up